{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Re-sign proof on a fresh rewrite of origin/tickets (2026-11-19 PST, rebar-session-3d705fec)\n\nOperator decision (2026-11-19, relayed by the coordinator): re-sign every failing event during the rewrite with the bot key on identity 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d's keyring when the event was written; the 253 events without `author_id` get 594c. Hold condition: enforced `verify-identity --all` (`REBAR_IDENTITY_REQUIRE_AUTHENTICATED=1`, no `enforce_since`) passes outright on the rewritten history, with reduced-state equality apart from the authorship and signature fields changed.\n\nImplementation: story `minimum-seedy-lowchen`, Gerrit 3470 (commit f2aadca6429, `make verify` green), not yet merged. Keys: SSM `/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key` versions 1-3 are PU4nHIqJCR (keyring add 2026-07-13 20:46 PDT), version 4 is oGCqzgfDMp (add 2026-09-07 15:39 PDT); exact public-key match against the keyring; neither revoked. Keys were loaded from SSM straight into a private, bounded ssh-agent; no private key was written to disk.\n\nRun: no-remote fetch of origin/tickets T1 = 49fcde8615f into /private/tmp/claude-502/bedbug-05f74084/proof1 (shadow `--git-dir` is its own `.git`, no remotes); boundary = 30-day first-parent horizon; published only to a file:// fake remote inside the workdir.\n\n| | original T1 | rewritten |\n|---|---|---|\n| commits | 311,348 | 13,838 |\n| blobless pack | 639,524 KiB | 111,240 KiB |\n| enforced verify-identity, non-verified | 8,326 (874 unsigned, 7,452 bad-signature) | **0** |\n\n- Re-sign plan matched all 8,326 failing events (raw files and SNAPSHOT ledger entries) and signed each with its era key before writing.\n- Reduced state: 10,393 tickets; 54,280 differing paths, 0 outside the allowed set: ledger `commit_sha` re-resolution 42,714 (by design of the collapse), ledger `signature` 4,988 and `signer_pubkey` 5,858, per-ticket `authorship` signed/unsigned counts 346+346, `author_id` 28.\n- enforce_since anchor 7a9d332fd62 is an ancestor of the new tip; fake remote holds only `refs/heads/tickets` (c29ce4e0d92) and the backup `refs/tickets-backup/pre-reclaim-20261120T010954Z` at T1.\n- First attempt failed closed before writing: 4 July 19 review-bot LINK events sit on a side branch that forked before the identity's CREATE, so no key is an ancestor on the original graph. After the collapse they share the checkpoint with the KEY_ADD and are ordered by position, which is what the verifier sees; the key choice now models the rewritten graph (test added).\n\nStep durations (seconds; host shared with a concurrent `make verify`): fetch T1 157, fake remote 142, shadow 181, reduce 70, blobless pack 189, enforced verify before 1,648, build re-sign plan 945, collapse 2,389, stamp epoch 3, publish to fake remote 55, pack after 14, enforced verify after 1,717, reduce after 17.\n\nNothing was published to origin; origin/tickets, the live tracker and the MCP box were not touched."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795139017410912001,"uuid":"61db6523-5866-4c65-ae86-c31d74959633"}